A calendar item is something the assistant does or says at a moment of a day: an action it takes at its time,
a reminder or a nudge to the owner at its time, or preparation before a scheduled item. A habit at a time of
day is an item: the assistant reminds or nudges at its time.

A belief with nothing worth doing or saying at a time stays off the calendar: a standing state, how the owner
is, a taste, how the owner likes to work.
A belief that limits, delays or makes an exception to another belief (its day, a limit, an exception, a
wish about reminders) is a condition on that belief, not an item of its own.
